				\begin{document}$${\bar{T}}_{{{\mathrm{BGC}}}+{{\mathrm{BGP}}}}$$\end{document}T¯BGC+BGP for the Bastin, Moustakis and Hurtt reforestation potentials compared to the baseline. A 15-year centered rolling mean was applied. Envelopes indicate the standard deviation (computed over 15-year rolling means) for the difference between the reforestation scenario and baseline across the five ensemble members. In (a), the grey bar shows the internal variability in the baseline simulation given by the one standard deviation spread across the five ensemble members from 2071 to 2100. Thicker line segments in (a, c) show where the response is statistically significant at the 90% level using the two-sample t-test, the thicker lines in (b) have been omitted as all years are statistically significant.

The \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
